CodexBar Linux
==============

CodexBar Linux is a Linux/Ubuntu port of the AI provider usage monitor
originally implemented for macOS as
  steipete/CodexBar  (https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar)
and ported to Windows as
  Finesssee/Win-CodexBar  (https://github.com/Finesssee/Win-CodexBar).

The Rust core in `crates/codexbar-core/` is a selective vendor of
`Finesssee/Win-CodexBar`'s `rust/` crate. Only the headless modules
(`core/`, `cli/`, `providers/{codex,claude,openai,openaiapi,openrouter}/`,
`status/`, `cost_scanner.rs`, `secure_file.rs`, `settings.rs`,
`logging.rs`) were copied. All Windows-specific and GUI modules were
omitted.

The upstream MIT LICENSE is preserved verbatim at
`crates/codexbar-core/LICENSE-WIN-CODEXBAR`. CodexBar Linux is
distributed under the same MIT terms (see `LICENSE` at repo root).

The Tauri desktop shell at `apps/desktop-tauri/` is original code for
this project: a thin Rust+JS layer that consumes the vendored core via
the `codexbar-core` crate, with no source lifted from upstream.
